Notebook[{
Cell["Answers to Selected Tutorial Problems", "Title"],

Cell["Tutorial 2, Q4", "Subtitle"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Define operators in vector calculus: divergence \[Del] \[CenterDot] A, \
curl \[Del] \[Cross] A, gradient ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[Del]f\)]],
  ", and Laplacian ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(\[Del]\^2 f\)\(.\)\)\)]],
  "  We  can use the following definitions which work in any dimensions \
except \[Del] \[Cross] A, which is specific to three dimensions.  Note that \
\[Del] = ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{
          FormBox[
            RowBox[{\(\[Sum]\+\(i = 1\)\%d\), 
              SubscriptBox[
                StyleBox["e",
                  FontWeight->"Bold"], "i"]}],
            "TraditionalForm"], \(\[PartialD]\_i\)}], TraditionalForm]]],
  ", where ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{
          SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["e",
              FontWeight->"Bold"], "i"], " "}], TraditionalForm]]],
  "is unit vector in ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`i\)]],
  "-th direction.  Also, ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\[Del]\^2 
          f = \[Del]\(\(\[CenterDot]\)\(\ \)\((\[Del]f)\)\)\)]],
  "."
}], "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(\(\( (*\ Vector\ calculus\ examples, \ 
      f\ for\ scalar, \ \((must\ be\ an\ explicit\ function\ of\ the\ \
coordinates)\), v\ for\ vector, \ \((represented\ as\ a\ list)\), \ 
      arg\ is\ a\ list\ of\ coordiates, \(\(.\)\(e\)\) . g, {x, y, 
        z}\ *) \)\(\[IndentingNewLine]\)\(\[IndentingNewLine]\)\(\(Div[v_, 
          arg_] := Inner[D, v, arg, Plus];\)\[IndentingNewLine]
    \(Curl[{v1_, v2_, v3_}, {x_, y_, z_}] := \ {D[v3, y] - D[v2, z], \ 
          D[v1, z] - D[v3, x], D[v2, x] - D[v1, y]};\)\[IndentingNewLine]
    \(Grad[f_, arg_] := \(D[f, #] &\) /@ arg\ ;\)\ \[IndentingNewLine]
    Laplacian[f_, arg_] := Div[Grad[f, arg], arg]\)\)\)], "Input"],

Cell["Tutorial 3, Q2 & 3", "Subtitle"],

Cell["\<\
The function func[ ] selects the entries in a list that are positive numbers. \
 The order of the elements are preserved.   It does this by moving the \
members of the first list to second list one by one in ff[ ].   Note that \
definitions will be applied recursively until none of the rules can be \
applied. \
\>", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[{
    \(\(func[l_] := ff[l, {}];\)\), "\n", 
    \(\(ff[{}, r_] := r;\)\), "\n", 
    \(\(ff[{h_, t___}, {r___}] := ff[{t}, {r, h}] /; h > 0;\)\), "\n", 
    \(ff[{h_, t___}, {r___}] := 
      ff[{t}, {r}] /; \((h \[LessEqual] 0 || 
            Head[h] \[Equal] Symbol)\)\)}], "Input"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(func[{1, 2, a, \(-3\), 7}]\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \({1, 2, 7}\)], "Output"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
The following program counts the repeated consecutive elements, producing a \
list of pairs of {element, count}. \
\>", "Text"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(runEncode[lst_List] := 
      Map[{#, 1} &, 
          lst] //. {u___, {v_, r_}, {v_, s_}, w___} \[Rule] {u, {v, r + s}, 
            w}\)], "Input"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(runEncode[{a, a, b, 1, 2, 2, 2, d}]\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \({{a, 2}, {b, 1}, {1, 1}, {2, 3}, {d, 1}}\)], "Output"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[StyleBox["", "Subtitle"]], "Subsubtitle"],

Cell["Tutorial 3, Q4", "Subtitle"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "The best way to read/write data that are in regular array or matrix form \
appears to be the command ",
  StyleBox["Import[ ]",
    FontFamily->"Terminal"],
  " and ",
  StyleBox["Export[ ]",
    FontFamily->"Terminal"],
  "."
}], "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
    \(\(?Export\)\)], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    RowBox[{"\<\"Export[\\\"file.ext\\\", expr] exports data to a file, \
converting it to a format corresponding to the file extension ext. \
Export[\\\"file\\\", expr, \\\"format\\\"] exports data to a file, converting \
it to the specified format.\"\>", " ", 
      ButtonBox[
        StyleBox["More\[Ellipsis]",
          "SR"],
        ButtonData:>"Export",
        Active->True,
        ButtonStyle->"RefGuideLink"]}]], "Print",
  CellTags->"Info3258874817-5707250"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["Tutorial 4, Q2", "Subtitle"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Quaternions are expressions of the form\n\t",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"a", " ", 
            StyleBox["1",
              FontWeight->"Bold"]}], " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"b", " ", 
            StyleBox["i",
              FontWeight->"Bold",
              FontSlant->"Plain"]}], "+", 
          RowBox[{"c", " ", 
            StyleBox["j",
              FontWeight->"Bold",
              FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
          StyleBox[" ",
            FontWeight->"Bold",
            FontVariations->{"CompatibilityType"->0}], "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"d", " ", 
            StyleBox["k",
              FontWeight->"Bold",
              FontSlant->"Plain"]}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
  "\nwhere ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{
          SuperscriptBox[
            StyleBox["i",
              FontWeight->"Bold",
              FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "=", 
          RowBox[{
            SuperscriptBox[
              StyleBox["j",
                FontWeight->"Bold",
                FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "=", 
            RowBox[{
              SuperscriptBox[
                StyleBox["k",
                  FontWeight->"Bold",
                  FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "=", 
              RowBox[{"-", 
                StyleBox["1",
                  FontWeight->"Bold"]}]}]}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
  ".  In addition, the product of ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{
          StyleBox["i",
            FontWeight->"Bold",
            FontSlant->"Plain"], ",", 
          StyleBox["j",
            FontWeight->"Bold",
            FontSlant->"Plain"], ",", 
          StyleBox["k",
            FontWeight->"Bold",
            FontSlant->"Plain"]}], TraditionalForm]]],
  "behaves like cross product of unit vector in three dimensions, such as ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
            StyleBox["i",
              FontWeight->"Bold",
              FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
            StyleBox["j",
              FontWeight->"Bold",
              FontSlant->"Plain"]}], " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"-", 
                StyleBox["j",
                  FontWeight->"Bold",
                  FontSlant->"Plain"]}], " ", 
              StyleBox["i",
                FontWeight->"Bold",
                FontSlant->"Plain"]}], "=", " ", 
            StyleBox["k",
              FontWeight->"Bold",
              FontSlant->"Plain"]}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
  ".  The question is the algebraic domain of the quaternions. "
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "It is clear that it is a ring: addition is a group, with ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{"0", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"0", " ", 
              StyleBox["1",
                FontWeight->"Bold"]}], "+", 
            RowBox[{"0", " ", 
              StyleBox["i",
                FontWeight->"Bold",
                FontSlant->"Plain"]}], "+", 
            RowBox[{"0", " ", 
              StyleBox["j",
                FontWeight->"Bold",
                FontSlant->"Plain"]}], "+", 
            RowBox[{"0", " ", 
              StyleBox["k",
                FontWeight->"Bold",
                FontSlant->"Plain"]}]}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
  " the additive identity.  Multiplication is distributive over addition.  \
The multiplicative identity is ",
  StyleBox["1",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  ".  Most importantly, multiplication is associative.   To show this we just \
need to show that the basis are associative: e.g.,\n\t",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"(", 
                RowBox[{
                  StyleBox["i",
                    FontWeight->"Bold",
                    FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
                  StyleBox["j",
                    FontWeight->"Bold",
                    FontSlant->"Plain"]}], ")"}], " ", 
              StyleBox["k",
                FontWeight->"Bold",
                FontSlant->"Plain"]}], " ", "=", " ", 
            RowBox[{
              RowBox[{
                StyleBox["k",
                  FontWeight->"Bold",
                  FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
                StyleBox["k",
                  FontWeight->"Bold",
                  FontSlant->"Plain"]}], " ", "=", " ", 
              RowBox[{"-", 
                StyleBox["1",
                  FontWeight->"Bold"]}]}]}], ","}], TraditionalForm]]],
  " ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
              StyleBox["i",
                FontWeight->"Bold",
                FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
              RowBox[{"(", 
                RowBox[{
                  StyleBox["j",
                    FontWeight->"Bold",
                    FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
                  StyleBox["k",
                    FontWeight->"Bold",
                    FontSlant->"Plain"]}], ")"}]}], " ", "=", " ", 
            RowBox[{
              RowBox[{
                StyleBox["i",
                  FontWeight->"Bold",
                  FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
                StyleBox["i",
                  FontWeight->"Bold",
                  FontSlant->"Plain"]}], " ", "=", " ", 
              RowBox[{"-", 
                StyleBox["1",
                  FontWeight->"Bold"]}]}]}], ","}], TraditionalForm]]],
  " so  ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{
                StyleBox["i",
                  FontWeight->"Bold",
                  FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
                StyleBox["j",
                  FontWeight->"Bold",
                  FontSlant->"Plain"]}], ")"}], " ", 
            StyleBox["k",
              FontWeight->"Bold",
              FontSlant->"Plain"]}], " ", "=", 
          StyleBox[" ",
            FontWeight->"Bold",
            FontSlant->"Italic"], 
          RowBox[{
            StyleBox["i",
              FontWeight->"Bold",
              FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
            RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{
                StyleBox["j",
                  FontWeight->"Bold",
                  FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
                StyleBox["k",
                  FontWeight->"Bold",
                  FontSlant->"Plain"]}], ")"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
  " also\n\t",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"(", 
                RowBox[{
                  StyleBox["i",
                    FontWeight->"Bold",
                    FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
                  StyleBox["i",
                    FontWeight->"Bold",
                    FontSlant->"Plain"]}], ")"}], " ", 
              StyleBox["k",
                FontWeight->"Bold",
                FontSlant->"Plain"]}], " ", "=", " ", 
            RowBox[{"-", " ", 
              StyleBox["k",
                FontWeight->"Bold",
                FontSlant->"Plain"]}]}], ",", " "}], TraditionalForm]]],
  " ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
              StyleBox["i",
                FontWeight->"Bold",
                FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
              RowBox[{"(", 
                RowBox[{
                  StyleBox["i",
                    FontWeight->"Bold",
                    FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
                  StyleBox["k",
                    FontWeight->"Bold",
                    FontSlant->"Plain"]}], ")"}]}], " ", "=", " ", 
            RowBox[{
              RowBox[{
                StyleBox["i",
                  FontWeight->"Bold",
                  FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
                RowBox[{"(", 
                  RowBox[{"-", 
                    StyleBox["j",
                      FontWeight->"Bold",
                      FontSlant->"Plain"]}], ")"}]}], " ", "=", " ", 
              RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"-", 
                  RowBox[{"(", 
                    RowBox[{
                      StyleBox["i",
                        FontWeight->"Bold",
                        FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
                      StyleBox["j",
                        FontWeight->"Bold",
                        FontSlant->"Plain"]}], ")"}]}], " ", "=", " ", 
                RowBox[{"-", 
                  StyleBox["k",
                    FontWeight->"Bold",
                    FontSlant->"Plain"]}]}]}]}], ","}], TraditionalForm]]],
  " so  ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{
                StyleBox["i",
                  FontWeight->"Bold",
                  FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
                StyleBox["i",
                  FontWeight->"Bold",
                  FontSlant->"Plain"]}], ")"}], " ", 
            StyleBox["k",
              FontWeight->"Bold",
              FontSlant->"Plain"]}], " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{
            StyleBox["i",
              FontWeight->"Bold",
              FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
            RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{
                StyleBox["i",
                  FontWeight->"Bold",
                  FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
                StyleBox["k",
                  FontWeight->"Bold",
                  FontSlant->"Plain"]}], ")"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
  ", and \n\t",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"(", 
                RowBox[{
                  StyleBox["i",
                    FontWeight->"Bold",
                    FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
                  StyleBox["j",
                    FontWeight->"Bold",
                    FontSlant->"Plain"]}], ")"}], " ", 
              StyleBox["i",
                FontWeight->"Bold",
                FontSlant->"Plain"]}], " ", "=", "  ", 
            RowBox[{
              RowBox[{
                StyleBox["k",
                  FontWeight->"Bold",
                  FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
                StyleBox["i",
                  FontWeight->"Bold",
                  FontSlant->"Plain"]}], " ", "=", 
              StyleBox["j",
                FontWeight->"Bold",
                FontSlant->"Plain"]}]}], ",", " "}], TraditionalForm]]],
  " ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
              StyleBox["i",
                FontWeight->"Bold",
                FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
              RowBox[{"(", 
                RowBox[{
                  StyleBox["j",
                    FontWeight->"Bold",
                    FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
                  StyleBox["i",
                    FontWeight->"Bold",
                    FontSlant->"Plain"]}], ")"}]}], " ", "=", " ", 
            RowBox[{
              RowBox[{
                StyleBox["i",
                  FontWeight->"Bold",
                  FontSlant->"Plain"], 
                StyleBox[" ",
                  FontWeight->"Bold",
                  FontSlant->"Plain"], 
                RowBox[{"(", 
                  RowBox[{"-", 
                    StyleBox["k",
                      FontWeight->"Bold",
                      FontSlant->"Plain"]}], ")"}]}], " ", "=", " ", 
              RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"-", 
                  RowBox[{"(", 
                    RowBox[{
                      StyleBox["i",
                        FontWeight->"Bold",
                        FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
                      StyleBox["k",
                        FontWeight->"Bold",
                        FontSlant->"Plain"]}], ")"}]}], " ", "=", " ", 
                StyleBox["j",
                  FontWeight->"Bold",
                  FontSlant->"Plain"]}]}]}], ","}], TraditionalForm]]],
  " so  ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{
                StyleBox["i",
                  FontWeight->"Bold",
                  FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
                StyleBox["j",
                  FontWeight->"Bold",
                  FontSlant->"Plain"]}], ")"}], " ", 
            StyleBox["i",
              FontWeight->"Bold",
              FontSlant->"Plain"]}], " ", "=", " ", 
          RowBox[{
            StyleBox["i",
              FontWeight->"Bold",
              FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
            RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{
                StyleBox["j",
                  FontWeight->"Bold",
                  FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
                StyleBox["i",
                  FontWeight->"Bold",
                  FontSlant->"Plain"]}], ")"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
  ", and \n\t",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"(", 
                RowBox[{
                  StyleBox["i",
                    FontWeight->"Bold",
                    FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
                  StyleBox["i",
                    FontWeight->"Bold",
                    FontSlant->"Plain"]}], ")"}], " ", 
              StyleBox["i",
                FontWeight->"Bold",
                FontSlant->"Plain"]}], " ", "=", " ", 
            RowBox[{"-", 
              StyleBox[" ",
                FontWeight->"Bold",
                FontSlant->"Italic"], 
              StyleBox["i",
                FontWeight->"Bold",
                FontSlant->"Plain"]}]}], ",", " "}], TraditionalForm]]],
  " ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
              StyleBox["i",
                FontWeight->"Bold",
                FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
              RowBox[{"(", 
                RowBox[{
                  StyleBox["i",
                    FontWeight->"Bold",
                    FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
                  StyleBox["i",
                    FontWeight->"Bold",
                    FontSlant->"Plain"]}], ")"}]}], " ", "=", " ", 
            RowBox[{
              RowBox[{
                StyleBox["i",
                  FontWeight->"Bold",
                  FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
                RowBox[{"(", 
                  RowBox[{"-", 
                    StyleBox["1",
                      FontWeight->"Bold"]}], ")"}]}], "  ", "=", " ", 
              RowBox[{"-", 
                StyleBox["i",
                  FontWeight->"Bold",
                  FontSlant->"Plain"]}]}]}], ","}], TraditionalForm]]],
  " so  ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{
                StyleBox["i",
                  FontWeight->"Bold",
                  FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
                StyleBox["i",
                  FontWeight->"Bold",
                  FontSlant->"Plain"]}], ")"}], " ", 
            StyleBox["i",
              FontWeight->"Bold",
              FontSlant->"Plain"]}], " ", "=", 
          StyleBox[" ",
            FontWeight->"Bold",
            FontSlant->"Italic"], 
          RowBox[{
            StyleBox["i",
              FontWeight->"Bold",
              FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
            RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{
                StyleBox["i",
                  FontWeight->"Bold",
                  FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
                StyleBox["i",
                  FontWeight->"Bold",
                  FontSlant->"Plain"]}], ")"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
  ", and so on.  I believe all the 3\[Cross]3\[Cross]3=27 cases can be \
verified."
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "It is not a field since elements don't commute.  However, each nonzero \
element has an inverse.  Let us give an explicit formula for inverse.   \
Consider\n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"a", " ", 
              StyleBox["1",
                FontWeight->"Bold"]}], " ", "+", " ", 
            RowBox[{"b", " ", 
              StyleBox["i",
                FontWeight->"Bold",
                FontSlant->"Plain"]}], "+", 
            RowBox[{"c", " ", 
              StyleBox["j",
                FontWeight->"Bold",
                FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
            StyleBox[" ",
              FontWeight->"Bold",
              FontVariations->{"CompatibilityType"->0}], "+", " ", 
            RowBox[{"d", " ", 
              StyleBox["k",
                FontWeight->"Bold",
                FontSlant->"Plain"]}]}], 
          StyleBox[")",
            FontWeight->"Bold",
            FontSlant->"Plain"]}], TraditionalForm]]],
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"a", " ", 
                StyleBox["1",
                  FontWeight->"Bold"]}], " ", "-", " ", 
              RowBox[{"b", " ", 
                StyleBox["i",
                  FontWeight->"Bold",
                  FontSlant->"Plain"]}], "-", 
              RowBox[{"c", " ", 
                StyleBox["j",
                  FontWeight->"Bold",
                  FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
              StyleBox[" ",
                FontWeight->"Bold",
                FontVariations->{"CompatibilityType"->0}], "-", 
              RowBox[{"d", " ", 
                StyleBox["k",
                  FontWeight->"Bold",
                  FontSlant->"Plain"]}]}], 
            StyleBox[")",
              FontWeight->"Bold",
              FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
          StyleBox["=",
            FontWeight->"Plain"], 
          RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
              SuperscriptBox[
                StyleBox["a",
                  FontWeight->"Plain"], "2"], "+", \(b\^2\), "+", \(c\^2\), 
              "+", \(d\^2\)}], " ", "=", " ", \(\(R\^2\)\(.\)\)}]}], 
        TraditionalForm]]],
  "\nThe cross terms vanish due to, e.g., ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
              StyleBox["i",
                FontWeight->"Bold",
                FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
              StyleBox["j",
                FontWeight->"Bold",
                FontSlant->"Plain"]}], " ", "+", " ", 
            RowBox[{
              StyleBox["j",
                FontWeight->"Bold",
                FontSlant->"Plain"], " ", 
              StyleBox["i",
                FontWeight->"Bold",
                FontSlant->"Plain"]}]}], " ", "=", " ", "0."}], 
        TraditionalForm]]],
  "   Divide ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`R\^2\)]],
  " to both sides of the above equation, as long as ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`R\)]],
  " is not zero, we find:\n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{
          SuperscriptBox[
            RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"a", " ", 
                  StyleBox["1",
                    FontWeight->"Bold"]}], " ", "+", " ", 
                RowBox[{"b", " ", 
                  StyleBox["i",
                    FontWeight->"Bold",
                    FontSlant->"Plain"]}], "+", 
                RowBox[{"c", " ", 
                  StyleBox["j",
                    FontWeight->"Bold",
                    FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
                StyleBox[" ",
                  FontWeight->"Bold",
                  FontVariations->{"CompatibilityType"->0}], "+", " ", 
                RowBox[{"d", " ", 
                  StyleBox["k",
                    FontWeight->"Bold",
                    FontSlant->"Plain"]}]}], 
              StyleBox[")",
                FontWeight->"Bold",
                FontSlant->"Plain"]}], \(-1\)], "="}], TraditionalForm]]],
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"a", " ", 
                StyleBox["1",
                  FontWeight->"Bold"]}], " ", "-", " ", 
              RowBox[{"b", " ", 
                StyleBox["i",
                  FontWeight->"Bold",
                  FontSlant->"Plain"]}], "-", 
              RowBox[{"c", " ", 
                StyleBox["j",
                  FontWeight->"Bold",
                  FontSlant->"Plain"]}], 
              StyleBox[" ",
                FontWeight->"Bold",
                FontVariations->{"CompatibilityType"->0}], "-", 
              RowBox[{"d", " ", 
                StyleBox["k",
                  FontWeight->"Bold",
                  FontSlant->"Plain"]}]}], 
            StyleBox[")",
              FontWeight->"Bold",
              FontSlant->"Plain"]}], "/", 
          RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{
                SuperscriptBox[
                  StyleBox["a",
                    FontWeight->"Plain"], "2"], "+", \(b\^2\), "+", \(c\^2\), 
                "+", \(d\^2\)}], ")"}], "."}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
  "\n\nAnother representation of the quaternions is to identify the basis \
with the matrices (related to Pauli matrices):\n\t",
  StyleBox["1",
    FontWeight->"Bold"],
  "=",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{"(", GridBox[{
              {"1", "0"},
              {"0", "0"}
              }], ")"}], TraditionalForm]]],
  ",  ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{
          StyleBox["i",
            FontWeight->"Bold",
            FontSlant->"Plain"], "=", 
          RowBox[{"(", GridBox[{
                {"i", "0"},
                {"0", "i"}
                }], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
  ",  ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{
          StyleBox["j",
            FontWeight->"Bold",
            FontSlant->"Plain"], "=", 
          RowBox[{"(", GridBox[{
                {"0", "1"},
                {\(-1\), "0"}
                }], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
  ",  ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{
          StyleBox["k",
            FontWeight->"Bold",
            FontSlant->"Plain"], "=", 
          RowBox[{"(", GridBox[{
                {"0", "i"},
                {"i", "0"}
                }], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]]],
  ",     ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`i = \@\(-1\)\)]],
  "\nThen the addition and multiplication correspond to matrix addition and \
multiplication."
}], "Text"],

Cell["Tutorial 4, Q3.", "Subtitle"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "This question discusses the relationship between polynomials modulo ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\((1 + x\^2)\)\)]],
  " and complex number ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\((a + b\ i)\)\)]],
  ".  Such polynomials are always of the form\n\t",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a\  + \ b\ x\)]],
  ",   ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a, \ b\  \[Element] \ R\)]],
  "\nAddition forms an Abelian group with 0 as additive identity.  \
Multiplication identity is 1.  Each nonzero element has an inverse:  The \
argument is similar to Q2.  Since we have\n\t",
  Cell[BoxData[{
      \(TraditionalForm\`\((a + b\ x)\)\ \((\ 
            a\  - \ b\ x)\)\ mod\ \((1 + x\^2)\)\  = \ 
        a\^2 - \(b\^2\) x\^2\ mod\ \((1 + x\^2)\)\), "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(=\)\(\ \)\(a\^2 + b\^2\)\)\)}]],
  "\nThus ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\((a + b\ x)\)\^\(-1\)\ mod\ \((1 + 
              x\^2)\)\  = \ \((a - b\ x)\)/\((a\^2 + b\^2)\)\ mod\ \((1 + 
              x\^2)\)\)]],
  ".   We have used the fact that ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`x\^2\ mod\ \((1 + x\^2)\)\  = \ \(-1. \)\)]],
  "  Association and distribution are automatic for polynomials.  So it forms \
a field. "
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "We can identify a linear polynomial ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a + b\ x\)]],
  " with a vector ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\((a, b)\)\)]],
  ".  The set of these vectors form a linear vector space.  In a linear \
vector space, we can add\n ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\((a, b)\) + \((c, d)\) = \((a + c, b + d)\)\)]],
  ".  \n We can multiply vector with a number\n \[Lambda] ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\((a, \ 
          b)\)\  = \ \((\[Lambda]\ a, \ \[Lambda]b)\)\)]],
  ".  \n Zero vector is (0,0), and two basis vectors of the space can be \
choosing to be (1,0) and (0,1).  At most two vectors are linearly \
independent.  Any vector can be expressioned as a linear combination of the \
basis.  The space is two dimensional."
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "We see that the rules for addition and multiplication for the polynomials \
mod ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\((1 + x\^2)\)\)]],
  " is exactly the same as that for complex numbers:\n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\((a + b\ x)\)\  + \ \((c\  + \ d\ x)\)\  = \ \((a + 
              c)\)\  + \ \((b + d)\) 
            x\ , \[IndentingNewLine]\((a + b\ x)\)\ *\((c + 
              d\ x)\)\ \  = \ \((a\ c\  - \ 
              b\ d)\)\  + \ \((b\ c + a\ d)\)\ \(\(x\ \ \ \ \ \ \ [
                mod\ \((1 + x\^2)\)]\)\(.\)\)\)]],
  "\nFor complex number, we have\n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\((a + b\ i)\)\  + \ \((c\  + \ d\ i)\)\  = \ \((a + 
              c)\)\  + \ \((b + d)\) 
            i\ , \n\((a + b\ i)\)\ *\((c + d\ i)\)\ \  = \ \((a\ c\  - \ 
              b\ d)\)\  + \ \((b\ c + 
                a\ d)\)\ i\ , \ \ \ i\  = \ \(\(\@\(-1\)\)\(.\)\)\)]],
  "\nWhere ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a, b, c, \(\(d\)\(\ \)\(\[Element]\)\(\ \)\)\)]],
  "R.  Thus the mapping from polynomial ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\((a + b\ x)\)\)]],
  " to the set of complex number ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\((a + i\ b)\)\)]],
  ", identifying the real part of the complex number with the constant term \
",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a\)]],
  " and imaginary part with ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(b\)\(\ \)\)\)]],
  "the coefficient of ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`x\)]],
  ", is a one-to-one and onto mapping.  Thus the field of polynomials mod ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\((1 + x\^\(\(2\)\(\ \)\))\)\)]],
  " and the complex number C are isomorphic to each other."
}], "Text"],

Cell["Tutorial 5, Q2", "Subtitle"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Consider Gaussian integers of the form\n\tG: ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a + b\ i\)]],
  ",  ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a, \ b\  \[Element] \ Z, \)]],
  " ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`i = \@\(-1\)\)]],
  ".\nWe want to show that it is an Euclidean domain."
}], "Text"],

Cell["\<\
(a) To show that Gaussian integers form a ring, we note that addition is \
closed and is an Abelian group, with 0 as additive identity.  Multiplication \
is associative (since this is so for complex numbers).  The multiplicative \
identity is 1.  Multiplication is distributive over addition.\
\>", "Text"],

Cell["\<\
Cancellation law is valid for complex numbers, so it is also valid for \
Gaussian integers. Thus the set of Gaussian integers form an integral domain.\
\
\>", "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "We now need to see how to do division with Gaussian integers, such that\n\t\
",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a = 
        b\ q\  + \ 
          r, \ \ \ \ \ \(\(|\)\(r\)\(|\)\(\ \)\(\(<\)\(\ \
\)\(\(|\)\(b\)\(|\)\)\)\), \ \ \ \ a, \ b, \ 
      q, \ \(\(r\)\(\ \)\(\[Element]\)\(\ \)\)\)]],
  "G.\nWe try to find the answer in C.  Let denote ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a\ b\^\(-1\) = \(\(c\  + \ 
            i\ d\)\(\ \ \)\(\[Element]\)\)\)]],
  "C, where ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`c\)]],
  " and ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`d\)]],
  " are real numbers. We separate out a nearest integer part and a fractional \
part for ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`c\)]],
  " and ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`d\)]],
  ":\n\t",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`c\  = \ 
        c\_I + c', \ \ \ \(\(|\)\(c'\)\(|\)\(\ \)\(\(\[LessEqual]\)\(\ \)\(1/
            2\)\)\), \[IndentingNewLine]d = \ 
        c\_I + d', \ \ \ \ \ \(\(|\)\(d'\)\(|\)\(\ \)\(\(\[LessEqual]\)\(\ \)\
\(1/2\)\)\), \)]],
  "\nwhere ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`c\_I\)]],
  ", ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`d\_I\)]],
  " \[Element] Z.  This is possible as a given real number is at most  1/2 \
away from the nearest integer.  Let the quotient ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`q = \ c\_I + i\ d\_I\)]],
  ", then ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a - b\ q\  = \ r\)]],
  " must be in G.  This is obvious since ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(a\)\(,\)\)\)]],
  " ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`b\)]],
  " and ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`q\)]],
  " are in G, and G is a ring.   We only need to show ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(\(|\)\(r\)\(|\)\(\ \)\(\(<\)\(\ \
\)\(\(|\)\(b\)\(|\)\)\)\)\(:\)\)\)]],
  "  \n\t",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(|\)\(r\)\(|\)\)\  = \ \(\(\(|\)\(a - 
              b\ q\)\(|\)\) = \(\(\(|\)\(b(c + \ i\ d)\  - \ 
                b\ q\)\(|\)\)\  = \ \(\(\(|\)\(b || 
                  c' + i\ \
d'\)\(|\)\(\[IndentingNewLine]\)\(\(\[LessEqual]\)\(\ \)\(\(|\)\(b\)\(|\)\(\ \
\)\(\@\(\((1/2)\)\^2 + \((1/2)\)\^\(\(2\)\(\ \)\)\)\)\)\)\) = \(\(|\)\(b\)\(|\
\)\(\(\(/\)\(\@2\)\)\(<\)\)\(|\)\(b\)\(|\)\(.\)\)\)\)\)\)]]
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "(b) Units are the numbers that have inverses.  Clearly\n\t",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`1*1 = 1\)]],
  ", ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\((\(-1\))\)*\((\(-1\))\)\  = \ 
        1, \ \ \ i*\((\(-i\))\)\  = 1\)]],
  ".\nThe units ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`u\)]],
  " in G are 1, ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(-1\), \ i, \ and\  - \(\(i\)\(.\)\)\)]],
  " Examples of primes are 2, 3, 5, 7, ..., ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`1 + i\)]],
  ", ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`1 - i, \ 3 + 5\ \(\(i\)\(.\)\)\)]],
  "  ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a\)]],
  " and ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`b\)]],
  " are associates of each other if ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a | b\)]],
  " and ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`b | a\)]],
  ".   Then ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a\)]],
  " and ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`b\)]],
  " must be related by  a unit ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`u\)]],
  ", i.e., ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a = u\ b\)]],
  ".   For examples, 3 and ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(-3\)\)]],
  " are associates, so is 3 and 3 ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(i\)\(.\)\)\)]],
  "  "
}], "Text"],

Cell["Tutorial 5, Q3.", "Subtitle"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Let work out the steps of extended Euclidean algorithm.  The division \
algorithm gives the recursive relation for remainder sequence:\n\t",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`r\_n\  - \ r\_\(n + 1\)\ q\_n = 
        r\_\(n + 2\); \ \ \ \ \ r\_0 = a, \ r\_1 = b, \ n = 0, \ 1, \ 
      2, \  ... \)]],
  "\n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`q\_n\)]],
  " is the quotient of ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`r\_n\)]],
  " divided by ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`r\_\(n + 1\)\)]],
  ".  We stop when the remainder becomes zero; the last nonzero remainder is \
the GCD.  Similarly\n\t",
  Cell[BoxData[{
      \(TraditionalForm\`s\_n\  - \ s\_\(n + 1\)\ q\_n = 
        s\_\(n + 2\); \ \ \ \ \ s\_0 = 1, \ s\_1 = 0, \ n = 0, \ 1, \ 
      2, \  ... \), "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      \(TraditionalForm\`t\_n\  - \ t\_\(n + 1\)\ \ q\_n = 
        t\_\(n + 2\); \ \ \ \ \ \ \ t\_0 = 0, \ t\_1 = 1, \ n = 0, \ 1, \ 
      2, \  ... \)}]],
  "\nsuch that \n\t",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`r\_n = a\ s\_n + \(\(b\)\(\ \)\(t\_n\)\(\ \)\)\)]],
  "   for ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`n\  = 0, \ 1, \ 2, \  ... \)]],
  "\nWe used a notation that is different from Algorithm 2.1 which makes \
thing clearer.  The important quantity to compute is ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`q\_n\)]],
  "."
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "We start with ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`r\_0 = \(a(x)\  = 
          4  x\^4 + 13  x\^3 + 15  x\^2 + 7  x + 1\)\)]],
  ", ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`r\_1 = \(b(x)\  = 2  x\^3 + x\^2 - 4  x - 3\)\)]],
  ", ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`s\_0 = 1, \ s\_1 = 0, \ t\_0 = 0, \ t\_1 = 1, \)]],
  " and compute ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(q\_0\)\(.\)\)\)]],
  "\n                              \n\t",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \)\(2  
          x\ \ \ \  + \ 11\/2\[IndentingNewLine]
      2  x\^3\  + \ x\^2\  - \ 4  x\  - \ 
        3\ \@\(\(4  x\^4\)\(\ \)\(+\)\(\ \)\(13  x\^3\)\(\ \)\(+\)\(\ \)\(15  \
x\^\(\(2\)\(\ \)\)\)\(+\)\(\ \)\(7  x\)\(\ \ \)\(+\)\(\ \ \)\(1\)\(\ \ \)\)\
\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ 4  x\^4\  + \ \ \ \ 2 
           x\^3\ \ \  - \ 8  x\^2\ \  - \ 6\ x\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \[HorizontalLine]\ \ \ \(\(\(\(\(\(\(\(\(\
\[HorizontalLine]--\)--\)--\)--\)--\)--\)--\)--\)--\) - \[IndentingNewLine]\ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ 11\ x\^\(\(3\)\(\ \
\)\)\ \ \  + 23\ x\^2\  + 13\ x\ \ \  + 1\ \[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ 11\
\ x\^3 + \ \(11\/2\) x\^2\  - 22  x\  - 33\/2\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \(--\(--\(--\(\
--\(--\(--\(--\(--\(--\[IndentingNewLine]\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \(35\/2\)\)\)\)\)\)\)\)\)\) 
          x\^2 + 35  x + 35\/2\)\)\)]]
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Thus, ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`q\_0 = 2  x + 11\/2\)]],
  ", ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`r\_2 = \(35\/2\) \((x\^2 + 2  x + 1)\)\)]],
  ", ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`s\_2 = \(s\_0 - \(s\_1\) q\_0 = 1\)\)]],
  ", ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`t\_2 = \ \(t\_0 - \(t\_1\) 
              q\_0 = \ \(\(-q\_0\) = \(-2\) x\  - 11\/2\)\)\)]],
  ".  We now do the second division:"
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "\n\t",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(\t\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \)\(\(4\/35\) x\  - 6\/35\[IndentingNewLine]
      \(35\/2\) x\^2\  + \ 35  x\  + \ 
        35\/2\ \@\(\(\ \)\(\(2  x\^3\)\(\ \)\(+\)\(\ \ \ \)\(x\^2\)\(\ \
\)\(-\)\(\ \)\(4 \( x\^\ \)\)\(-\)\(3\)\(\ \ \)\)\)\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ 2  x\^3\  + \ 4  x\^2\  + 
        2\ x\ \[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \[HorizontalLine]\ \ \ \(\(\(\(\(\(\
\[HorizontalLine]--\)--\)--\)--\)--\)--\)\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \(-3\) 
          x\^\(\(2\)\(\ \)\)\  - 6\ x\  - 3\ \[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \(-3\) 
          x\^2\  - 6  x\  - 3\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \(--\(--\(--\(\
--\(\(--\[IndentingNewLine]\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ 0\)\(\ \ \)\)\)\)\)\)\)\)\)]]
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Thus, ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`q\_1 = \(4\/35\) x - 6\/35\)]],
  ", ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`r\_3 = 0\)]],
  ", ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`s\_3 = \(s\_1 - \(s\_2\) q\_1 = \(0 - 
              1*q\_1 = \(-\(4\/35\)\) x + 6\/35\)\)\)]],
  ",  ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`t\_3 = \(t\_1 - \(t\_2\) q\_1 = \ 
          1\  - \(\((\(-2\) x - 11\/2)\)\(*\)\)\)\)]],
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\((\(4\/35\) x - 6\/35)\)\)]],
  "."
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(GCD(a(x), b(x))\)\(=\)\)\)]],
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(35\/2\) x\^2 + 35  x + 35\/2\)]],
  ",  ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`s(x) = \(s\_2 = 1\)\)]],
  ", ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`t(x) = \(t\_2 = \(-2\) x - 11\/2\)\)]],
  ".   ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`s(x)\)]],
  " and ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`t(x)\)]],
  " is such that we have ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`GCD(a(x), 
          b(x)) = \(s(x)\) \(a(x)\) + \(t(x)\) \(\(b(x)\)\(.\)\)\)]],
  "  We can verify:"
}], "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
    \(\(a = 
        4  x^4 + 13  x^3 + 15  x^2 + 7  x + 1;\)\), "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    \(\(b = 2  x^3 + x^2 - 4  x - 3;\)\), "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    \(\(s = 1;\)\), "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    \(\(t = \(-2\) x - 11/2;\)\), "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    \(\(gcd = 35/2  x^2 + 35  x + 35/2;\)\), "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    \(Simplify[gcd\  - \ a*s - b*t]\)}], "Input"],

Cell[BoxData[
    \(0\)], "Output"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["Tutorial 5, Q1", "Subtitle"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Given the following equations:\n\t",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`2  x + \ 4  y - 2  z = 
        1, \[IndentingNewLine]2  x + \ \ \ \ \ y\  + \ \ \ z = 
        3, \[IndentingNewLine]5  x\  - 3  y + 7  z = 0, \)]],
  "\nWe solve it first in Z",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\_3\)]],
  ", Z",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\_5\)]],
  ", Z",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\_7\)]],
  ", Z",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\_11\)]],
  ".   We can use either the positive representation (numbers range from 0 to \
",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`p - 1\)]],
  "),  or symmetric representation ( numbers from ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(-\((p - 1)\)\)/2\)]],
  " to ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\((p - 1)\)/2\)]],
  ").   I'll use positive presentation in solving the equations. "
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Z",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\_3\)]],
  ":\n\t",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`2  x + y + z = 1, \[IndentingNewLine]2  x + y + z = 
        0, \[IndentingNewLine]2  x\ \  + \ z\  = \ 0. \)]],
  "\nThe system is inconsistent, as the first two equations has the same \
coefficients but different right-hand side.  There is no solution.   In any \
case the determinant ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`d\  \[Congruent] 0\ \ \(\((mod\ 3)\)\(.\)\)\)]],
  "\t"
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Z",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\_\(\(5\)\(:\)\)\)]],
  "\n\t",
  Cell[BoxData[{
      \(TraditionalForm\`2  x + 4  y + 3  z = 1, \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \((1)\)\), 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      \(TraditionalForm\`2  x + y + z\  = \ 
        3, \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \((2)\)\), "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      \(TraditionalForm\`0\ x\  + 2  y + 2  z\  = 
        0. \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \((3)\)\)}]],
  "\nTo be able to preserve the value of determinant we use only steps that \
don't multiply a number to an equation.  First, we replace (2) by  ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\((2)\)\(-\)\)\)]],
  "(1), get\n\t[2\t4\t3\t1]\n\t[0\t2\t3\t2]\t(because ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`1 - 4 \[Congruent] \(-3\) \[Congruent] 
        2\ mod\ 5\)]],
  ")\n\t[0\t2\t2\t0]\t\nNow we do ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\((3)\)\(-\)\)\)]],
  "(2), we get\n\t[2\t4\t3\t1]\n\t[0\t2\t3\t2]\n\t[\t0\t4\t3]\t(because ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`2 - 3 \[Congruent] \(-1\) \[Congruent] 
        4\ mod\ 5\)]],
  ")\nso the determinant is obtained from the product of the diagonal \
elements ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`d\  \[Congruent] 2*2*4 \[Congruent] 16 \[Congruent] 
        1\ mod\ \ 5\)]],
  ".  Using the backward substitution step, we get \n\t ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`z \[Congruent] \((4\^\(-1\)*3)\)\  \[Congruent] \ 
        4*3 \[Congruent] 12 \[Congruent] 
        2\ mod\ 5, \[IndentingNewLine]y \[Congruent] 
        2\^\(-1\)*\((2 - 3  z)\) \[Congruent] 
        3*\((2 - 3*2)\) \[Congruent] \(-12\) \[Congruent] 
        3  mod\ 5, \[IndentingNewLine]x \[Congruent] 
          2\^\(-1\)*\((1 - 3  z - 4  y)\)\  = \ 4\ mod\ 5. \)]],
  "\nThe values for ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`d\_x = x\ d\  \[Congruent] \ 4, \ 
      d\_y = y\ d \[Congruent] 3, \ d\_z = z\ d \[Congruent] 2, \)]],
  " all mod 5."
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "The steps for Z",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\_7\)]],
  "and Z",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\_11\)]],
  " are similar.  We find the following results (ignore the case of ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`p = 3\)]],
  "):\n",
  Cell[BoxData[{
      \(TraditionalForm\`\
p\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ d\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ d\
\_x\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ d\_y\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ d\_z\), 
    "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      \(TraditionalForm\`\
5\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ 1\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ 4\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ 3\
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ 2\), "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      \(TraditionalForm\`\
7\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ 6\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ 0\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ 0\
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ 4\), "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      \(TraditionalForm\`\
11\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ 6\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ 10\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ 8\
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ 1\)}]]
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Using the Chinese remainder theorem, we reconstruct solutions in Z for the \
4 quantities ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`d, \ d\_x, \ d\_y, \ \(\(d\_z\)\(.\)\)\)]],
  "   For example, using the mix-radix expansion, let\n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`d\  = \ v\_0 + \(v\_1\) 5 + \(v\_2\) 5*7\)]],
  ".\nIn mod 5,  we get  ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`d\ mod\ 5\  = \ \(1\  = \ v\_0\)\)]],
  ".   In mod 7, we have ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`d\ mod\ 7\  = \ \(v\_0 + \(v\_1\) 5\  = \ \(1 + 
              5  v\_1 = \ 6\)\)\)]],
  ".   So ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`v\_1 = \ \(\(5\^\(-1\)\) \((6 - 1)\) = \(3*5 = 
            1\ mod\ 7\)\)\)]],
  ".  Inverse of 5 in mod 7 is 3, since  ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(3*5\)\(=\)\)\)]],
  " 15 \[Congruent] 1 mod 7.   In mod 11, we get ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`6 = 1 + 1*5 + v\_2*5*7\)]],
  ", or  ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`0 = \(v\_2\) 5*7\)]],
  ", so ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`v\_2 = 0. \)]],
  "   Thus ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`d \[Congruent] \ 6\ mod\ \((5*7*11)\)\  = \ 
        6\ mod\ \ 385. \)]]
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "Similarly for ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`d\_x\)]],
  ", we get  ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`v\_0 = \ 4\)]],
  ".  In mod 7, we get  0 = 4 + ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(v\_1\) 5\)]],
  ", so ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`v\_1 = \(\(5\^\(-1\)\) \((\(-4\))\) = \(3*\((\(-4\))\
\) \[Congruent] \(-12\) = 2\ mod\ 7. \)\)\)]],
  "   In mod 11, we have ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`10 = 4 + 2*5 + v\_2*35\)]],
  ",  or ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`v\_2 = \ \(\((35)\)\^\(-1\)\) \((\(-4\))\) \
\[Congruent] \(2\^\(-1\)\) \((\(-4\))\) \[Congruent] 
          6*\((\(-4\))\) \[Congruent] 9\ mod\ 11\)]],
  ".   Thus ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`d\_x = \(4 + 2*5 + 9*5*7 = 
          329 \[Congruent] \(-56\)\ mod\ 385\)\)]],
  ".   The second number is in symmetric representation.  To be able to \
handle negative solutions in equations, the final answers have to be in the \
symmetrical representation.   Go through the steps for ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`d\_y\)]],
  "and ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`d\_z\)]],
  ", we find:\n\t",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`d = 6, \ \ \ d\_x = \(-56\), \ \ \ d\_y = 
        63, \ \ \ d\_z = 67\)]],
  "     (mod 385).\nThus the solution for ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`x, y, z\)]],
  " in Q is (due to Cramer's rule)\n\t",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`x = \(d\_x/
            d = \(\(-\(56\/6\)\) = \(-\(28\/3\)\)\)\), \[IndentingNewLine]y = \
\(d\_y/d = \(63\/6 = 21\/2\)\), \[IndentingNewLine]z = \(d\_z/
            d = \(\(67\/6\)\(.\)\)\)\)]]
}], "Text"],

Cell["Tutorial 6.  Q3.", "Subtitle"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "We compute the square-free factorization of the polynomial with \
coefficient in Z",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\_2\)]],
  "\n\t",
  Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
        RowBox[{\(b(x)\), "=", 
          
          RowBox[{\(x\^10 + x\^6 + x\^5 + x\^3 + x\^2 + 1\), "      ", 
            "\[Element]", "  ", 
            RowBox[{
              SubscriptBox[
                StyleBox["Z",
                  FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "[", "x", "]"}]}]}], 
        TraditionalForm]]],
  "."
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "The steps for square-free factorization are:\n\tLet ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a = \ \(\(a\_1\) a\_2\^2\ a\_3\^3 ... \) 
          a\_k\^k\)]],
  " (",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a\_j\)]],
  "are square-free factor),\n\t(1)  compute ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(c = \(GCD(a, a') = \(\(a\_2\) a\_3\^2 ... \) 
              a\_k\^\(k - 1\)\);\)\)]],
  "\n\t(2)  compute factor of ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(a\)\(,\)\)\)]],
  "  ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`w = \(a/c = \(\(a\_1\) \(a\_2\) a\_3 ... \) 
            a\_k\)\)]],
  ";\n\t(3)  compute another GCD,  ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`y = \(GCD(w, c) = \(\(a\_2\) a\_3 ... \) a\_k\)\)]],
  ";\n\t(4)  the first factor is given by ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`z = \(w/y = a\_1\)\)]],
  ";\n\t(5)  Let ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a\  \[LeftArrow] \ c\)]],
  ", repeat step (1) to (4),  last step is then ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`GCD(a, a') = \(\(unit\)\(.\)\)\)]],
  "\n\t(6) If ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(a' = 0\)\(,\)\)\)]],
  " do ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a \[LeftArrow] a\^\(1/p\)\)]],
  " and factor ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(a\)\(.\)\)\)]]
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "First iteration: \n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a = a(x), \ 
      a' = \(b' \((x)\) = 
          10  x\^9 + 6  x\^5 + 5  x\^4 + 3  x\^2 + 2  x \[Congruent] \ 
            x\^4 + x\^2\ \ \ mod\ 2\)\)]],
  ".\n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`c = \(GCD(a, 
            a') = \(\(GCD(x\^10 + x\^6 + x\^5 + x\^3 + x\^2 + 1, 
              x\^4 + x\^2)\)\(.\)\)\)\)]],
  "\nTo compute the above GCD, we do long division mod 2.\n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \)\(x\^6\ \  + x\^4\  + x\[IndentingNewLine]
      x\^4 + 
        x\^2\ \ \ \@\(x\^10\ \ \ \ \ \  + \ \ \ \ \ \ \ x\^6 + x\^5 + x\^3 + \
x\^2 + 1\)\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ x\^10 + 
        x\^8\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ ___  ___  ___  ___  ___  ___  ___ \
 ___  __\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ x\^8\ \ \  + \ x\^6\  + x\^5 + x\^3 + x\^2 + 1\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ x\^8\ \ \  + \ x\^6\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ __\ \ \ \ _\
__  ___  ___  ___  ___  ___  _\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ x\^5 + x\^3 + 
        x\^2\ \  + \ 1\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ x\^5 + 
        x\^3\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ ___  ___  ___  ___  ___\
\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ x\^2\  + \ 1\)\)\)]],
  "\t\n(note that  ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`1 \[Congruent] \(-1\)\ mod\ 2, \ 
      2 \[Congruent] 0\ mod\ 2\)]],
  ").\nContinuing with the Euclidean algorithm, we have:\n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \)\(x\^2\[IndentingNewLine]
      x\^2 + 1\ \ \ \ \ \ \@\(x\^4\ \ \  + \ \ \ x\^2\)\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ x\^4\ \ \ \  + \ \ \
x\^2\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ ___  ___  __\
\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ 0\)\)\)]],
  "\nThus ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`c = \(GCD(a, a') = x\^2 + 1. \)\)]],
  "\n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`w = a/\(\(c\)\(:\)\)\)]],
  "\n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(\[IndentingNewLine]\)\(\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \)\(x\^8\ \  + x\^6\  + x\^3\  + 
        1\[IndentingNewLine]
      x\^2 + 
        1\ \ \ \@\(x\^10\ \ \ \ \ \  + \ \ \ \ \ \ \ x\^6 + x\^5 + x\^3 + \
x\^2 + 1\)\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ x\^10 + 
        x\^8\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ ___  ___  ___  ___  ___  ___  ___ \
 ___  __\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ x\^8\ \ \  + \ x\^6\  + x\^5 + x\^3 + x\^2 + 1\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ x\^8\ \ \  + \ x\^6\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ __\ \ \ \ _\
__  ___  ___  ___  ___  ___  _\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ x\^5 + x\^3 + 
        x\^2\ \  + \ 1\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ x\^5 + 
        x\^3\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ ___  ___  ___  ___  ___\
\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ x\^2\  + \ 1\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ x\^2 + \ 1\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ ___  ___\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ 0\)\)\)]],
  "\nso ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`w = x\^8 + x\^6 + x\^3 + 1\)]],
  ".\nNow ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`y = \(GCD(w, 
            c) = \(\(GCD(x\^8 + x\^6 + x\^3 + 1, \ x\^2 + 1)\)\(:\)\)\)\)]],
  "\n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \)\
\(x\^6\ \  + x\[IndentingNewLine]
      x\^2 + 
        1\ \ \ \@\(x\^8\ \ \  + \ \ x\^6\  + \ x\^3\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \  \
+ \ 1\)\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ x\^8\ \  + \ \ \ x\^6\
\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ ___  ___  ___  ___  ___  ___  __\
\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ x\^3\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \  + 
        1\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ x\^3\ \  + x\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ __\ \ \ \ _\
__  ___  ___  ___  __\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ x\ \ \ \ \  + \ \
\ 1\)\)\)]],
  "\nContinue with the division:\n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \)\(x\ \ \
\  + \ 1\[IndentingNewLine]
      x + 1\ \@\(x\^2\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \  + \ 1\)\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ x\^2\  + x\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ ___  ___  ___  _\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ x\ \ \ \ \
\  + \ 1\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ x\ \ \ \ \
\  + \ 1\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ ___  ___  _\
\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ 0\)\)\)]],
  "\nSo ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`y = \(GCD(w, c) = 1 + x\)\)]],
  ".  Thus the first factor ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`z = \(w/
            y = \(a\_1 = \((x\^8 + x\^6 + x\^3 + 1)\)/\((1 + x)\)\)\)\)]],
  ".\n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \)\(x\^7 \
+ x\^6\  + x\^2\  + x\ \  + \ 1\[IndentingNewLine]
      x + 
        1\ \@\(x\^8\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \  + x\^6 + x\^3\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \  + 1\)\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ x\^8 + x\^7\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ ___  ___  ___  ___  ___  ___  ___  __\
\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ x\^7 + 
        x\^6\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ x\^7 + 
        x\^6\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ ___  ___  ___  ___  \
___  ___  __\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ x\^3\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \  + 1\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ x\^3 + x\^2\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ ___  ___  ___  ___\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ x\^2\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \  + 1\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ x\^2 + 
        x\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ ___  ___  ___\
\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ x\ \  + \ 1\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ x\ \  + \ 1\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ ___  __\[IndentingNewLine]
      \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \
\ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ \ 0\)\)\)]],
  "\nSo ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a\_1 = \ x\^7 + x\^6 + x\^2 + x + 1\)]],
  "."
}], "Text"],

Cell[TextData[{
  "We have finished first iteration.  Now we enter second iteration for \
computation of ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a\_2\)]],
  ".   Let ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a = \(c = x\^2 + 1\)\)]],
  ",  the new ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`c = \(GCD(a, a') = \(GCD(x\^2 + 1, \ 0) = 
            x\^2 + 1\)\)\)]],
  ".   We are in trouble because the derivative of ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a\)]],
  " (which is ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`2  x\)]],
  ")  is zero  (in mod 2).   Thus we have to evoke step (6).   We write \n\t\
",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a = \(\((x\^2 + 1)\)\  = \ \((b(x))\)\^2\)\)]],
  ",\nand find the polynomial ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`b(x)\)]],
  ".  Since ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a\)]],
  " is quadratic, so ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`b(x)\)]],
  " must be linear.   There are only 4 linear polynomial in Z",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\_2\)]],
  ", there are 0, 1, ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(x\)\(,\)\)\)]],
  " ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`x + 1\)]],
  ".   Clearly\n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\((1 + x)\)\^2 \[Congruent] \ 
        x\^2 + 1\ \ mod\ 2\)]],
  ".  Since ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`1 + x\)]],
  " can not be factored further, we conclude that ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`\(\(a\_2 = 1\)\(,\)\)\)]],
  " and ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a\_3 = \((1 + x)\)\)]],
  ".   This is because old ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`c\)]],
  " during the first iteration (new ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a\)]],
  " in second iteration) is ",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`c = \(a\_2\) a\_3\^2\)]],
  ".\nThe final result for square-free factorization is \n",
  Cell[BoxData[
      \(TraditionalForm\`a(
          x)\  = \ \((x\^7 + x\^6 + x\^2 + x + 1)\) \((x + 1)\)\^3\)]],
  "."
}], "Text"]
},
FrontEndVersion->"4.2 for Microsoft Windows",
ScreenRectangle->{{0, 1280}, {0, 941}},
WindowSize->{680, 856},
WindowMargins->{{277, Automatic}, {Automatic, 9}},
